  "limitations": [
    "Independent source followup and counterevidence only; six actual public images plus reports/manifests, no models and no newly accepted or production-ready scene. This archive is separate from the paused source-screening-increment receipt and does not retry that denied action.",
    "The moon-island interview image is an 864x478 third-party embedded still, not a native decoded video frame. A different performer pose and clearer local details still give a nearly frontal view, with no usable independent side/top spatial baseline.",
    "Five hotel-screening images preserve three near-coaxial red-piano images, an existing seaside-bar reference and one low-angle snow-mountain hotel clue. Neither multiple poses nor titles establish distinct camera angles, complete rooms or new geometry.",
    "The hotel date association is producer-recorded public-page adjacency evidence, not a verified native clip time. The single close low view, missing wide/second view and occlusion remain insufficient for reconstruction.",
    "Producer screening records 103 URLs, 101 received files and 98 fully decoded images; three truncated files and two missing downloads were not promoted to successes. Only the six relevant complete images in this frozen package are archived here.",
    "Recorded HTTP 403, robots/nonretryable and inaccessible/login-shell outcomes remain preserved as research limits. Archive worker does not retry those sources, browse videos, copy credentials or change security settings.",
    "Exact supplied file bytes, SHA256, Git blobs, original objects and the real independent commit are verified. Six image manifest entries and decoded dimensions are checked, without upgrading their source identity or geometry claims.",
    "New archive and original-history refs plus research/source-followup-20261105 isolate this package. Every preexisting branch and base-tree path is retained. No modeling, rendering, source-script execution, force push, LFS, main edits, Issues or PRs; all Space temporaries remain for dot to manage."
  ],
